        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                "word": "tortillon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5e97a309-b9ea-44c8-8ca7-8b1bc58c905c",
                        "entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "tortillons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7eaa96d6-2b46-31ad-ae62-c2079486b8af",
                        "entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chose tortillée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3345fb1-d4d8-4e0b-91cb-35302bed62d3",
                                "sense_id": "7eaa96d6-2b46-31ad-ae62-c2079486b8af",
                                "text": "Un tortillon de papier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c19e7620-a315-4b9f-b595-1a7c4f7b463e",
                                "sense_id": "7eaa96d6-2b46-31ad-ae62-c2079486b8af",
                                "text": "Un tortillon de paille."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d08ce400-5142-4190-8fbc-9ecbd8e43d8c",
                                "sense_id": "7eaa96d6-2b46-31ad-ae62-c2079486b8af",
                                "text": "Et les oreilles ! ah ! les oreilles ! On tortillait un bout de serviette et on l’y entrait jusqu’au fond, comme on enfonce un foret, comme on plante un tire-bouchon…\nLe petit tortillon était enfoncé si vigoureusement que j’en avais les amygdales qui se gonflaient ; le tympan en saignait, j’étais sourd pour dix minutes, on aurait pu me mettre une pancarte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b00453b-fa44-4ec9-a6b5-8033e545e397",
                                "sense_id": "7eaa96d6-2b46-31ad-ae62-c2079486b8af",
                                "text": "Le dessert vint – il arrive toujours – composé d’une banane et d’un minuscule pot de crème. La jeune fille aux bas bleus avait commencé à lui servir son pauvre régal ; mais il lui prit le pot des mains et arrosa sa banane à sa manière, qui était un tortillon en huit de chiffres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e667fd2e-ac91-4cba-9e73-c5487e253690",
                                "sense_id": "7eaa96d6-2b46-31ad-ae62-c2079486b8af",
                                "text": "Lili tenait à la main une grosse cigale dans l’arrière de laquelle ils avaient planté, par un tortillon pointu, un petit éventail de papier. Cependant, Paul grattait sur une pierre une allumette soufrée.\nIls avaient évidemment l’intention de mettre le feu à ce gouvernail avant de lancer la bestiole dans les airs."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4ad388ff-9701-3e4d-a0ef-eedb917a10ee",
                        "entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Linge tortillé en bourrelet qu'on met sur la tête pour porter un fardeau."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2fc6b77f-ced1-3ad8-b02a-fe2d22512377",
                        "entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petit chignon fait d’une tresse de cheveux tordue et roulée sur elle-même."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b7875956-dd6d-386f-887d-8b873aa0bdda",
                        "entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Déjection de lombric ; turricule."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f69ba6e5-6b98-3420-9ae9-86379015436a",
                        "entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Très jeune tortue (mâle ou femelle)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e08ddd97-b7e3-4c32-b9ee-886dffd3533f",
                                "sense_id": "f69ba6e5-6b98-3420-9ae9-86379015436a",
                                "text": "Pour les tortues marines, le terme “tortillon” est souvent utilisé pour désigner les bébés, indépendamment de leur espèce."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "de384b03-ae05-4d0e-8da7-d5491541d961",
                        "source_entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
                        "source_sense_description": "Très jeune tortue",
                        "target_lang_word": "turtlet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "turtlet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                        "entry_id": "015c429e-c553-30a4-a856-8e160629a14b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small or baby turtle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5aac0b4c-901b-41dc-b454-274562a368b2",
                                                "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                                "text": "The turtlet scurried across the sandy beach, its tiny legs moving quickly as it searched for a safe place to hide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9730973-ad5a-4be0-949d-99e63b3ad1b1",
                                                "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                                "text": "Only recollect when, off Ceylon, I picked up that pretty little turtlet, which you all contended was a log of wood,—but I knew he was a turtle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bb3331e-bd21-4ec9-bdeb-fb2dd5b111b2",
                                                "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                                "text": "Of course comparatively very few individuals of a brood of several dozen Turtlets reach maturity, but they meet with their death through Sea-birds, Crocodiles, Sharks, and similar enemies, which in all probability swallow them regardless of the number of disposition of their victims' scutes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f65824af-59b3-4dcc-9d7c-05d6eec6d9a0",
                                                "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                                "text": "Imagine a dark mite of a turtlet struggling to the surface in the middle of a huge expanse of white sand over and on which numerous enemies are lurking. It behooves the mite to get to the sea as soon as possible, but how can it know which way to go?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8e77380-3d4e-4194-82f2-e7efa66e504a",
                                                "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                                "text": "She craned forward to watch exactly what happened and saw that the turtlet in the centre of the three was moving its head slowly from side to side."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e5d3e99-03fb-4464-a183-03a3bf0a4023",
                                                "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                                "text": "Soon, about 30 young turtlets are circling the illuminated hatching point; the light from our guide's lamp acts as a fence, keeping them grouped together."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e89a7e8e-02d6-4ee7-a5b6-0bb7f188489c",
                                                "sense_id": "fc205782-231c-3066-bb38-ca30483ccd35",
                                                "text": "Bull sharks have the strongest bite of any measured shark and can eat turtlets as well as other bull sharks and probably have no problem ripping open a canoe like a can of salted mackerel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3a441d26-037a-48af-b559-2aa65aeb420f",
                        "source_entry_id": "c75958e2-6719-3056-82e5-ea078c18aaed",
